# Display Kconfig
# LVGL is now provided as a managed component (lvgl/lvgl via idf_component.yml).
# LVGL's own Kconfig is exposed automatically by the component manager.

config CORE2FORAWS_LCD_DRAW_BUF_LINES
    int "LVGL draw buffer height (display lines)"
    depends on SOFTWARE_DISPLAY_SUPPORT
    range 10 60
    default 20
    help
      Height, in display lines, of each LVGL draw buffer. The driver allocates
      two of these (double buffering) as RGB565, so the internal DMA-capable
      DRAM cost is:

          lines * 320 * 2 bytes * 2 buffers

      At the default of 20 lines that is 25,600 bytes, and each buffer needs a
      single *contiguous* 12,800-byte DMA block. Contiguity, not total free
      heap, is what typically fails once Wi-Fi and BLE are running.

      Larger values reduce the number of partial transfers per frame and raise
      throughput. Lower this if display initialization reports insufficient
      DMA-capable DRAM; raise it if your application leaves internal DRAM to
      spare.

      These buffers must stay in internal DRAM; PSRAM is not DMA-addressable
      and is not a fallback. See the memory budget section of the BSP README.
